    "instructions.closing": "That's it! With Automatic Mode on, you don't need to record anything manually — Checking takes care of it for you.",
    "instructions.heading": "Instructions",
    "instructions.intro": "This guide walks you through using Checking: recording attendance manually, enabling Automatic Mode (location-based check-in/check-out), and setting up the Scheduled Pause.",
    "instructions.step1.item1": "On the home screen, type your 4-character key in the 'Key' field. It glows orange when the key is found.",
    "instructions.step1.item2": "Type your password in the 'Password' field. On success the fields turn green and 'Authentication completed' appears.",
    "instructions.step1.item3": "If you don't have a password yet, the app opens password setup automatically; if the key doesn't exist, it offers self-registration.",
    "instructions.step1.title": "1. Sign in",
    "instructions.step2.item1": "Pick 'Check-In' or 'Check-Out' and the type 'Normal' or 'Backdated'.",
    "instructions.step2.item2": "With Automatic Mode off, select the 'Location' from the list and tap 'Register Check-In' (or 'Check-Out').",
    "instructions.step2.item3": "The card at the top shows your last check-in and check-out; tap it to see the full list with date, time and location.",
    "instructions.step2.title": "2. Record attendance manually",
    "instructions.step3.callout": "Important: for reliable background operation, grant Location as 'Allow all the time' and disable battery optimization for Checking.",
    "instructions.step3.item1": "Tap the gear (next to the key/password fields) to open 'Settings'.",
    "instructions.step3.item2": "Tap 'Automatic Activities' and tick the 'Enable Automatic Activities' box.",
    "instructions.step3.item3": "Grant each permission in the list by tapping it: Notifications, Location 'all the time' (Allow always), Battery unrestricted and — on some devices — 'Start with device'.",
    "instructions.step3.item4": "When the gear glows GREEN, Automatic Mode is active and healthy. An ORANGE glow means a recommended permission is missing.",
    "instructions.step3.lead": "With Automatic Mode, the app checks you in and out on its own, based on your location — when you enter or leave a registered area, when you foreground the app, and on periodic checks.",
    "instructions.step3.title": "3. Enable Automatic Mode",
    "instructions.step4.item1": "In 'Settings', tap 'Scheduled Pause'.",
    "instructions.step4.item2": "Turn it on and set the 'From' and 'To' times (for example, 22:00 to 06:00).",
    "instructions.step4.item3": "Optionally, also tick 'Suspend on Saturdays' and/or 'Suspend on Sundays'.",
    "instructions.step4.item4": "During the pause the app performs no automatic activity; it resumes on its own at the end of the period.",
    "instructions.step4.lead": "The Scheduled Pause saves battery by suspending automatic activities during a period (for example, overnight).",
    "instructions.step4.title": "4. Enable the Scheduled Pause",
    "instructions.step5.item1": "Tap 'LAST CHECK-IN' or 'LAST CHECK-OUT' to open the table with the Date, Time and Location of each record.",
    "instructions.step5.item2": "Records made near but outside a registered area show as 'Localização não Cadastrada' (unregistered location).",
    "instructions.step5.item3": "Even with no internet, your records are saved on the device and sent as soon as the connection returns, always with the original time.",
    "instructions.step5.title": "5. Track your history",
    "instructions.step6.item1": "Tap 'Transport' to open the personnel transport module.",
    "instructions.step6.item2": "Enter the address and time you need and submit the request.",
    "instructions.step6.item3": "The logistics manager organizes the trips; an artificial-intelligence engine suggests how to group passengers and order the stops.",
    "instructions.step6.title": "6. Request transport",
    "instructions.step7.item1": "Any user can open Accident Mode; it notifies, in real time, every user on the same project.",
    "instructions.step7.item2": "Report your situation and zone: 'safe', 'at the accident site but safe', or 'at the accident site and needing help'.",
    "instructions.step7.item3": "If possible, record a video of the site: it is sent in real time to the administrator's dashboard.",
    "instructions.step7.item4": "The 'Call Emergency Service' button calls the local emergency service, reporting the accident and location in the region's language.",
    "instructions.step7.lead": "Accident Mode is a safety feature. Use it only in a real emergency.",
    "instructions.step7.title": "7. In case of an accident",
    "instructions.step8.item1": "'Alerts': choose which notifications you receive (activities, scheduled pause, accident).",
