    "manual.heading": "Usage Instructions",
    "manual.highlights.accessBody": "The app decides automatically when to ask for user registration, password creation, or regular authentication.",
    "manual.highlights.accessTitle": "Guided access",
    "manual.highlights.locationBody": "Permissions, GPS accuracy, and manual fallback directly influence the attendance workflow.",
    "manual.highlights.locationTitle": "Tracked location",
    "manual.highlights.supportBody": "Settings centralizes language, password, location, WhatsApp support, and access to this documentation.",
    "manual.highlights.supportTitle": "Fast help",
    "manual.introPrimary": "This manual summarizes the main authentication, attendance, location, transport, and support flows of Checking Web.",
    "manual.introSecondary": "Use this page as a quick reference to understand what the application handles automatically and which actions remain under user control.",
    "manual.sections.accident.item1": "Any user can open Accident Mode; it alerts, in real time, every user on the same project.",
    "manual.sections.accident.item2": "Report your situation and zone: safe, at the accident site but safe, or at the accident site and needing help. If possible, record a video of the site — it is sent in real time to the administrator dashboard.",
    "manual.sections.accident.item3": "The Trigger Emergency Service button calls the local emergency service, reporting the accident and location in the regional language.",
    "manual.sections.accident.lead": "Accident Mode is a safety feature. Use it only in a real emergency.",
    "manual.sections.accident.title": "In case of an accident",
    "manual.sections.attendance.figureCaption": "Example of a successful attendance registration state.",
    "manual.sections.attendance.item1": "The form distinguishes check-in from check-out and can block manual submission when automatic activities are controlling the flow.",
    "manual.sections.attendance.item2": "Visible history near the top helps confirm the last recorded event before sending a new one.",
    "manual.sections.attendance.item3": "Success or failure messages appear in the status area after each attempt.",
    "manual.sections.attendance.lead": "With valid authentication, the user selects the registration type, reviews the context, and submits the operation from the main screen.",
    "manual.sections.attendance.title": "Check-in and check-out",
    "manual.sections.authFlow.item1": "If the key does not exist, the flow moves into user registration without waiting for another click.",
    "manual.sections.authFlow.item2": "If the key exists but still has no password, the interface opens password registration directly.",
    "manual.sections.authFlow.item3": "If the key and password already exist, the interface stays on the normal login path.",
    "manual.sections.authFlow.lead": "The application checks the key status as soon as it reaches four valid characters and decides which assistance flow to show.",
    "manual.sections.authFlow.note": "Closing a modal manually does not create an endless loop: the system only tries again when the key or the relevant auth state really changes.",
    "manual.sections.authFlow.title": "Authentication flow",
    "manual.sections.automaticActivities.item1": "This mechanism depends on valid authentication, location readings, and internal rules that avoid unsafe transitions.",
    "manual.sections.automaticActivities.item2": "When automatic activities are controlling the flow, some manual fields become hidden or disabled to protect record consistency.",
    "manual.sections.automaticActivities.item3": "If precision drops below the required threshold, the app may re-enable manual fallback options instead of making a risky assumption.",
    "manual.sections.automaticActivities.lead": "The app can also trigger check-in, check-out, and related updates when location context changes in the expected way.",
    "manual.sections.automaticActivities.title": "Automatic activities",
    "manual.sections.faq.a1": "This happens when the key does not exist or when the account still has no password. The new flow removes extra clicks and takes the user straight to the correct action.",
    "manual.sections.faq.a2": "Because the application already understands that precise permission is active, or because a location refresh is already running.",
    "manual.sections.faq.a3": "First confirm that the key and password were authenticated. If the problem continues, open Support so your key can be sent to the support team.",
    "manual.sections.faq.lead": "Use these quick answers when the interface feels stuck or when the flow is not progressing as expected.",
    "manual.sections.faq.q1": "Why did the app open a registration flow by itself?",
    "manual.sections.faq.q2": "Why is the Allow Location button disabled?",
    "manual.sections.faq.q3": "What should I do if Transport does not open?",
    "manual.sections.faq.title": "Common problems and FAQ",
    "manual.sections.location.figureCaptionDenied": "Example of the screen when location permission is still unavailable.",
    "manual.sections.location.figureCaptionGranted": "Example of the screen after precise location access is granted successfully.",
    "manual.sections.location.item1": "The application depends on HTTPS, browser support, and active permission to request precise location.",
    "manual.sections.location.item2": "When permission is denied or unavailable, the app shows clear messages and can limit the flow to the allowed manual fallback.",
    "manual.sections.location.item3": "When location is obtained successfully, the interface updates accuracy, recognized place, and related automatic actions.",
    "manual.sections.location.lead": "The device position is used to determine operational context, trigger automatic flows, and guide the user when accuracy is not yet good enough.",
    "manual.sections.location.title": "Location permission and GPS behavior",
    "manual.sections.login.item1": "The password can still be validated automatically by the existing main-shell flow.",
    "manual.sections.login.item2": "If the user changes the typed password after authenticating, the app protects itself again until the new value is verified.",
    "manual.sections.login.item3": "Status messages help distinguish \"waiting for password\", \"verifying\", and \"authenticated\".",
    "manual.sections.login.lead": "Users who already exist type the key, enter the password, and let the app validate authentication before recording attendance or opening Transport.",
    "manual.sections.login.title": "Login",
    "manual.sections.overview.figureCaption": "Checking Web main shell with the authentication area and attendance form.",
    "manual.sections.overview.item1": "The main screen shows the key, password, recent history, attendance form, and the shortcut to Transport.",
    "manual.sections.overview.item2": "Assistance flows appear automatically when the key does not exist yet or when the user still needs to create the first password.",
    "manual.sections.overview.item3": "The Settings menu groups secondary actions so the main area stays compact.",
    "manual.sections.overview.lead": "Checking Web combines authentication, attendance registration, location context, and transport access in a single mobile-first surface.",
    "manual.sections.overview.title": "Overview",
    "manual.sections.passwordChange.figureCaption": "Password-change flow opened from Settings > Change Password.",
    "manual.sections.passwordChange.item1": "Open Settings, tap Change Password, and use the existing password-change modal.",
    "manual.sections.passwordChange.item2": "The flow asks for old password, new password, and confirmation while preserving the current validations.",
    "manual.sections.passwordChange.item3": "The action stays enabled only when the user is authenticated and already has a registered password.",
    "manual.sections.passwordChange.lead": "Password change is no longer placed in the main authentication row and now lives inside Settings.",
    "manual.sections.passwordChange.title": "Reset or change password",
    "manual.sections.passwordRegistration.figureCaption": "First-password creation modal for a user that already exists in the system.",
    "manual.sections.passwordRegistration.item1": "The modal reuses the existing password component, but hides the old-password field.",
    "manual.sections.passwordRegistration.item2": "The user enters the new password, confirms the value, and completes the first access.",
    "manual.sections.passwordRegistration.item3": "After saving, the backend authenticates the web session and the main screen accepts the remaining operations.",
    "manual.sections.passwordRegistration.lead": "If the key already exists but no password is registered yet, Checking Web enters first-password creation mode.",
    "manual.sections.passwordRegistration.title": "Automatic password registration",
    "manual.sections.projectSelection.figureCaption": "Example of the projects block in the authenticated shell, showing the active scope summary.",
    "manual.sections.projectSelection.item1": "During registration, the user marks one or more valid projects before completing account creation.",
    "manual.sections.projectSelection.item2": "After authentication, the main panel shows current projects and allows updates when that capability is enabled.",
    "manual.sections.projectSelection.item3": "The active project influences location lists, contextual history, and other user-scoped surfaces.",
    "manual.sections.projectSelection.lead": "The app uses projects both during initial registration and in the daily workflow to limit user context and available locations.",
    "manual.sections.projectSelection.title": "Project selection",
    "manual.sections.scheduledPause.item1": "In Settings, tap Scheduled Pause.",
    "manual.sections.scheduledPause.item2": "Enable the option and set the From and To times (for example, 10:00 PM to 6:00 AM).",
    "manual.sections.scheduledPause.item3": "Optionally also enable Suspend on Saturdays and/or Suspend on Sundays. During the pause the app performs no automatic activity and resumes on its own when the period ends.",
    "manual.sections.scheduledPause.lead": "Scheduled Pause saves battery by suspending automatic activities during a chosen period (for example, at night).",
    "manual.sections.scheduledPause.title": "Scheduled Pause",
    "manual.sections.settings.figureCaption": "Settings widget with the new centralized secondary actions.",
    "manual.sections.settings.item1": "Language updates the visible labels of the main application and keeps the preference in browser storage.",
    "manual.sections.settings.item2": "Allow Location reuses the existing pipeline to request precise access again when that is still needed.",
    "manual.sections.settings.item3": "Support and About use the same entry point to open WhatsApp and this documentation.",
    "manual.sections.settings.lead": "The gear icon opens a central place for preferences and secondary actions without crowding the authentication row.",
    "manual.sections.settings.title": "Settings",
    "manual.sections.support.item1": "The link uses the official phone number configured in the Checking Web frontend.",
    "manual.sections.support.item2": "The initial message is prepared automatically to reduce friction and speed up support.",
    "manual.sections.support.item3": "If no valid key is available, the support button stays disabled for safety.",
    "manual.sections.support.lead": "When the user needs human help, Settings > Support prepares a WhatsApp conversation with the user key already included in the first message.",
    "manual.sections.support.title": "Support",
    "manual.sections.transport.figureCaption": "Example of the Transport surface opened from the Checking Web shell.",
    "manual.sections.transport.item1": "Access stays protected by the same key and password validated in the main shell.",
    "manual.sections.transport.item2": "The module includes address registration, per-type requests, and a summary of the current status.",
    "manual.sections.transport.item3": "When a vehicle is allocated, the screen shows the main operational details for the user.",
    "manual.sections.transport.lead": "After authentication, the user can open the Transport module to request rides, inspect status, and review the most recent request details.",
    "manual.sections.transport.title": "Transport access",
    "manual.sections.userRegistration.figureCaption": "New-user registration modal opened automatically for an unknown key.",
    "manual.sections.userRegistration.item1": "The form asks for key, full name, projects, optional email, password, and password confirmation.",
    "manual.sections.userRegistration.item2": "Projects are loaded from the API and the user can mark one or more valid items.",
    "manual.sections.userRegistration.item3": "After a successful submission, the web session is authenticated and the app stays unlocked for use.",
    "manual.sections.userRegistration.lead": "When the key does not exist in the database, the app opens the self-service form so a new user can complete registration.",
    "manual.sections.userRegistration.title": "Automatic user registration",
